\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,084 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2010\par 12:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA SAYS "NOT SUITABLE2 TO MEET JAPAN PRIME MINISTER AT UN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beijing said Tuesday the atmosphere was "not suitable" for a meeting between the premiers of China and Japan on the sidelines of a U.N. summit in New York, amid a deep rift over an incident at sea. (published 0717 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UK AUGUST PSNB GBP15.3 BLN, INTEREST COSTS SOAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. public sector borrowed significantly more than expected in August, as higher debt interest payments pushed central government spending sharply higher, the Office for National Statistics said Tuesday. (published 1017 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UK TREASURY'S TAYLOR: NEED PROPORTIONATE FINANCIAL REGULATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A senior U.K. Treasury official reiterated Tuesday the importance of the financial district to the U.K. economy, stressing the need for "proportionate" regulation to avoid hampering financial innovation. (published 0941 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SAFE OFFICIAL: CHINA SHOULDN'T FEAR A FLOATING EXCHANGE RATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China shouldn't fear a floating exchange rate as it considers reform of the yuan exchange-rate mechanism, a senior official with the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulator wrote in a recent essay, adding the yuan's current narrow trading band has hindered development of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. (published 0416 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RBA SAYS INTEREST RATES HAVE MORE WORK TO DO ON INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  is on track to raise interest rates soon, saying Tuesday if its current central scenario for the economy eventuates, the monetary policy brakes will need to be tapped again. (published 0242 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ABARE EXPECTS AUSTRALIAN GDP TO GROW 3.00% IN 2010-11 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's chief commodities forecaster on Tuesday modestly lowered its forecast for economic growth in the fiscal year which began July 1 to 3.00% from a June forecast of 3.25%, saying that growth in domestic demand is expected to strengthen only gradually, although exports will be strong. (published 0000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB WELLINK: WON'T FORECAST BIG RISE IN MARKET RATES IN 4Q -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market interest rates across the euro zone shouldn't rise significantly in the fourth quarter, when the lion share of the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's outstanding loans to banks expire, ECB Governing Council member Nout Wellink said in an interview published Tuesday. (published 1033 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STATE BANK OF INDIA RAISES SHORT-TERM FUNDS; TIGHT LIQUIDITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the country's largest lender by assets, raised funds via short-term debt Tuesday, underscoring a cash crunch in the banking system that has pushed interbank lending rates higher. (published 1007 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA SECRETARY: CAPITAL INFLOWS NOT POSING PROBLEM FOR NOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW DELHI (Dow Jones)--Foreign capital inflows into India aren't posing any problems for now, but the authorities are keeping a close watch on signs of overheating in the capital markets, Finance Secretary \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ashok Chawla\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0810 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ABARE RAISES AUSTRALIA'S 2010-11 COMMODITY EXPORTS FORECAST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's resources boom has well and truly resumed, driven by surging iron ore and coal exports to booming Asian markets, according to the latest report by the Australian Bureau of Agricultural and Resource Economics. (published 0131 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : NO FURTHER MEASURES TO CURB BAHT FOR NOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  has no immediate plans to impose further measures to stem the baht's rise against the dollar as existing tools to manage capital inflows are already sufficient, Governor Tarisa Watanagase said Tuesday. (published 0437 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER: EXPECT PM TO EXPLAIN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO OBAMA IF NECESSARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan will explain the reasons behind his government's recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to U.S. President Barack Obama if \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  becomes a topic of conversation during their talks later this week, Japan's finance minister said Tuesday. (published 0136 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : EURO GAINS A LITTLE AS AUCTIONS SUCCEED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro and the yen are stronger Tuesday, the former because of successful bond and treasury bill auctions by euro-zone debtors and the latter because of end-of-quarter demand from Japanese exporters. (published 0955 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOCUS: DOLLAR TO ASCEND AS QEII DOESN'T \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Just as rising speculation over more quantitative easing drove the dollar down, so falling speculation should drive the dollar higher. Yes, risk sentiment, the performance of equity markets, the ups and downs of the euro-zone sovereign debt crisis have all played their part in the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent slide agaisnt the euro. (published 0714 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: DOLLAR TO RESUME DOWNWARD TREND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: The pair has rebounded on its rising trend line, and should post a further up move as the RSI is well directed. Suggests long positions above 1.3030, with 1.3125 and 1.3160 in sight. The downside breakout of 1.3030 will open the way to 1.3000 and 1.2955. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: SHORT TERM WEAKNESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The contracts stand below their declining trend lines. Intraday BUND: The contract is posting a rebound, but should strike against its resistance. Suggests short positions below 129.85, with 129.30 and 129.05 in sight. The upside penetration of 129.85 will call for a rebound towards 130.25 and 130.50. Weekly chart BUND trend: Bullish. (published 0640 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: HK IPO FEVER BOOSTS LOCAL RATES, HK DOLLAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hong Kong dollar is poised to rise in coming weeks toward the top end of its parity band against the U.S. dollar, driven by the latest rally in stocks and a jump in local rates on the territory's recent IPO fever. (published 0447 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: AUSTRALIAN DOLLAR TOUTING COULD LEAD TO POUTING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A sharp divergence of opinions on the Aussie dollar is developing between bears in Asia and bulls abroad - and the nature of that overseas trading means the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may fall quickly once the current wave of enthusiasm crests. (published 0404 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: NEW ZEALAND 2Q GDP TIPPED TO EXPAND 0.8% ON QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand economy likely continued to expand in the second quarter as the recovery gains traction. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: BOJ SEPTEMBER TANKAN LIKELY TO SHOW MODERATE IMPROVEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan's September tankan survey, due next Wednesday, will likely show that sentiment among big manufacturers continued picking up for the sixth consecutive quarter, but the surging yen and increasing uncertainty over the global economy are expected to have slowed the pace of the improvement. (published 0305 GMT) [ 21-09-10 1000GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100921e69l000sj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
