\par\par \b \uc2 INDIAN MORNING BRIEFING: Sensex May Rise To 20,050\b0\par\par\uc2 1,714 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2010\par 05:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Energy Service\par \uc2 NRG\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 South Korean markets are closed Tuesday for a holiday.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLOBAL MARKETS \par DJIA                10753.62  +145.77  +1.37% \par Nasdaq              2355.83   +40.22   +1.74% \par S&P 500             1142.71   +17.12   +1.52% \par FTSE 100            5602.54   +94.09   +1.71% \par Nikkei Stock        9664.52   +38.43   +0.40% \par Hang Seng           22049.44  +72.10   +0.33% \par Kospi               n/a       n/a      n/a \par SGX Nifty           6006.50   +2.50    +0.04% \par Sept. contract \par  \par USD/JPY             85.70-71     -0.03% \par Range               85.80-85.52 \par EUR/USD             1.3062-64     0.00% \par Range               1.3120-1.3028 \par  \par CBOT Wheat Dec.     $7.316 per bushel \par Comex Gold          $1,280.80    +$3.30 \par Comex Gold Range    $1,275.60-$1,285.20 \par Nymex Crude (NY)    $74.86       +$1.20 \par  \par  \par CHARTING THE SENSEX \f28 \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bombay Stock Exchange\uc2 's 30-share Sensitive Index could rise to 20,050, according to charts.\par \par \uc2 A short-term downward correction remains elusive as the Sensex continues to march ahead. Monday's sharp rise has pushed the index deeper into overbought territory. Despite no signs of any weakness as yet, there is a strong case for a quick downward correction.\par \par \uc2 A drop below minor support at 19,900 would lead to a fall to major support at 19,620.\par \par \uc2 The National Stock Exchange's 50-share Nifty could test resistance at 6,010.\par \par \uc2 Though minor support for the Nifty is at 5,960, the short-term trend would remain bullish until the index falls below major support at 5,860.\par \par \uc2 As long as the index trades above 5,860, there would be a strong case for a rise to major resistance at 6,080.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks rallied to their highest level in more than four months as encouraging financial and home-builder earnings boosted confidence in the economic recovery.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financials led the Dow Industrials Monday, after earnings from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Discover Financial Services\f28 \uc2 \f2  hinted at improving credit trends. Discover gained 3.8%. Leading blue chips, \f28 \uc2 \f2 American Express\f28 \uc2 \f2  gained 4.2%, while \f28 \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan Chase\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose 2.8% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2  climbed 2.5%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stocks' gains accelerated after the National Bureau of Economic Research, the unofficial arbiter of recessions' start and end dates, said the recession began in December 2007 and ended in June 2009.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We're beginning to get some indications it's more of a muddle-through economy in the U.S., rather than a double dip [recession]," said Sean Kraus, chief investment officer at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citizens Trust\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "There was so much negative news built into the markets that anything positive is good."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Home builders climbed Monday, ahead of a week packed with housing data, after Lennar's earnings beat analysts' expectations. Lennar climbed 8.2%, after it returned to profitability in the fiscal third quarter and earnings topped Street forecasts. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Home Depot\f28 \uc2 \f2  climbed 2.5%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ASIAN STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were higher Tuesday, buoyed by solid gains on Wall Street, with cyclical stocks advancing in Tokyo and Sydney.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Nikkei Share Average, Australia's S&P/ASX 200 and New Zealand's NZX-50 were all up. Markets in Seoul were closed for a public holiday. DJIA futures were down three points in screen trade.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors are awaiting the outcome of the Federal Reserve's policy meeting later Tuesday amid speculation that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may adopt further measures to stimulate the economy. Most analysts don't expect new quantitative easing measures from the Fed, but the speculation has helped lift U.S. bond prices and underpin demand for U.S. stocks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kazuhiro Takahashi, general manager at Daiwa Securities Capital Markets said investors were also wary on China-related stocks amid rising tension between Japan and China as Beijing Sunday suspended high-level contacts after Tokyo extended the detention of a boat captain accused of intentionally ramming his trawler into two Japanese patrol vessels.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese automakers, which have exposure to China, were struggling. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nissan Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose a modest 0.3% despite announcing plans to nearly double its annual capacity of vehicle production in China by 2012.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Honda Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2  was up 0.3%, while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2  lost 0.2%. Commodity shares were higher after gold futures set a new record high Monday; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sumitomo Metal Mining\f28 \uc2 \f2  advanced 0.8%, and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose 1.2%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cyclical stocks were helping the Sydney market higher. Major banks were up 0.7%-0.9%, while BHP Billiton added 0.7% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto\f28 \uc2 \f2  advanced 0.8%.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar was trading in tight ranges against the euro and the yen as investors remained cautious ahead of the outcome of the Fed meeting. The euro was fetching $1.3057 against the dollar, from $1.3061 late Monday in New York, and was at Y111.96 against the yen, from Y112.02. The dollar was buying Y85.72 compared with Y85.75.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par METALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold futures Monday settled at their third consecutive record high on speculation about further stimulative U.S. government action ahead of Tuesday's meeting of the Federal Reserve's rate-setting committee. Spot gold was at $1,278.40 per troy ounce, down 10 cents from Monday's New York close.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Base metals mostly closed marginally lower on the London Metal Exchange Monday as investors squared their books ahead of the Fed meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par OIL SUMMARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October Nymex crude oil futures were down 57 cents at $74.29 per barrel on Globex.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CALENDAR OF EVENTS Sept. 21 \par 0830 IST Mumbai:      \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bombay Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  chief executive at launch \par                       of BSE mobile trading \par 0900 IST New Delhi:   Federal new and renewable energy secretary, \par                       \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rural Electrification Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  finance director, \par                       \f28 \uc2 \f2 IDBI Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  chairman at renewable energy India \par                       forum \par 0930 IST New Delhi:   Junior defense minister, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tata Power\f28 \uc2 \f2  Strategic \par                       Electronics Division chief executive, Rolta \par                       Thales director for defense at seminar on \par                       battlefield management system \par 1000 IST New Delhi:   \f28 \uc2 \f2 Power Finance Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . annual shareholders' meeting \par 1130 IST Mumbai:      \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indian Oil Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . annual shareholders' meeting \par 1200 IST New Delhi:   Vertex Group chief executive, Vertex India chief \par                       executive at press meet \par 1215 IST New Delhi:   Federal steel secretary, TATA Steel chief \par                       resident executive, JSL director at Federation \par                       of Indian Chambers of Commerce and Industry \par                       interactive meet \par 1215 IST Gurgaon:     BMW India president at the launch of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BMW\f28 \uc2 \f2  X5 \par 1230 IST Mumbai:      \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ashoka Buildcon\f28 \uc2 \f2  chairman at initial public \par                       offering press meet \par N/A:                  MMTC annual shareholders' meeting \par 1145 GMT US:          Sept. 18 ICSC-\f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  chain store sales \par                       index \par 1230 GMT US:          August new residential construction - housing \par                       starts and building \par 1255 GMT US:          Sept. 18 Johnson Redbook retail sales index \par 1815 GMT US:          Federal Reserve Board - U.S. interest rate \par                       decision \par 1400 GMT US:          Treasury chief economist testifies before senate \par                       banking committee on investing in infrastructure: \par                       creating jobs and growing economy \par 1700 GMT US:          Treasury secretary hosts mortgage disclosure forum \par 2100 GMT US:          Sept. 19 ABC News consumer comfort index \par  \par  \par TOP HEADLINES - Dow Jones/WSJ \par RBA MINUTES: INTEREST RATES HAVE MORE WORK TO DO TO CONTAIN INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  is on track to raise interest rates soon saying Tuesday if its current central scenario for the economy eventuates, the monetary policy brakes will need to be tapped again. (published 0130 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ABARE EXPECTS AUSTRALIAN GDP TO GROW 3.00% IN 2010-11 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's chief commodities forecaster on Tuesday modestly lowered its forecast for economic growth in the fiscal year which began July 1 to 3.00% from a June forecast of 3.25%, saying that growth in domestic demand is expected to strengthen only gradually, although exports will be strong. (published 0000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EX-RESERVE BANK OF AUSTRALIA OFFICIAL TIPS RATE HIKE BY YEAR-END \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's new Australia Chief Economist Paul Bloxham--who just left the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's economic analysis department--Tuesday said it's likely monetary policy will be tightened again before year-end. (published 0101 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER: EXPECT PM TO EXPLAIN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO OBAMA IF NECESSARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan will explain the reasons behind his government's recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to U.S. President Barack Obama if \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  becomes a topic of conversation during their talks later this week, Japan's finance minister said Tuesday. (published 0136 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA STRATEGIC, PRIMUS, AIG AGREE TO ABORT NAN SHAN SALE PACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Strategic Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that it and its consortium partner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Primus Financial Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . have agreed with \f28 \uc2 \f2 American International Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to abort the consortium's attempts to purchase AIG's Taiwanese life-insurance unit effective immediately. (published 0015 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: SASKATCHEWAN PREMIER UNSWAYED BY BHP CEO ON POTASH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s chief executive has so far failed to sway Saskatchewan's top lawmaker to favor the mining giant's proposed $38.6 billion purchase of fertilizer maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Potash Corp. of Saskatchewan\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 2325 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 HEWLETT-PACKARD\f28 \uc2 \f2 , ORACLE SETTLE SUIT OVER HURD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hewlett-Packard Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Oracle Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday they had resolved litigation regarding former H-P Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mark Hurd\f28 \uc2 \f2 , who accepted a position as an \f28 \uc2 \f2 Oracle\f28 \uc2 \f2  co-president a month after resigning from the technology giant. (published 2253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =WSJ: NOKIA DELAYS NEW FLAGSHIP SMARTPHONE 'A FEW WEEKS' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 09-20-10 2306ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nokia Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has pushed back delivery of its much-delayed flagship smartphone by another few weeks, saying it needs the time to make final adjustments. (published 0138 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CANON: TO SPEND Y14.6 BLN ON NEW THAI INKJET PRINTER PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canon Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it will spend Y14.6 billion to construct an inkjet printer plant in Thailand to meet growing printer demand worldwide. (published 0120 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ANZ: CHINA REGULATOR OKS FIRM TO SET UP LOCALLY INCORPORATED ENTITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia & New Zealand Banking Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has received approval from China's banking regulator to set up a locally incorporated entity with an initial registered capital of CNY2.5 billion, the company said Tuesday. (published 0133 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TOP HEADLINES - Indian Media \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Essar Steel\f28 \uc2 \f2  Signs 10-Year Ore Deal With Orissa Miners - Economic Times \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indian Oil Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  Raises Gasoline Price INR0.27 A Liter - PTI \par Merck Unit Files Case Against India's Sun Pharmaceutical - Business Standard \par ITC Unlikely To Subscribe To EIH Rights Issue - Mint \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 09-20-10 2306ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62500   \par \par \uc2 Dokument NRG0000020100921e69l0000e\par }\page {\p