\par\par \b \uc2 Nikkei languishes, buoyed by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  wariness\b0\par\par\uc2 724 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2010\par 01:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Resistance holds near 9,600, level of 100-day MA\par \par \uc2 * Caution on more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  buoys Nikkei after dip\par \par \uc2 * Panasonic climbs after report of no stock issue\par \par \uc2 * Trade is thinnest in over a week\par \par \uc2 By Elaine Lies\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 22 (Reuters) - Japan's Nikkei stock average dipped on Wednesday, but losses were stemmed after the dollar edged back up towards the 85 yen level and by expectations that a strong yen rise would bring Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar slipped as low as 84.78 yen, taking the Nikkei with it, after the Federal Reserve's latest statement on the U.S. economy intensifed speculation that it would take more quantitative easing steps later this year.\par \par \uc2 But Prime Minister Naoto Kan was quoted by the Financial Times as saying that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets was "unavoidable" if there were drastic changes in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week carried out its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in six years, and market players said hope of more was keeping shares solidly supported.\par \par \uc2 "The downside is actually quite strong, stocks could easily have fallen a lot more," said Toshiyuki Kanayama, market analyst at \uc2 Monex Inc\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Basically there's a lot less worry about the possibility of a stronger yen, since the market now expects that any trend in that direction will bring more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In that sense, the psychological impact of last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still helping."\par \par \uc2 The dollar stood at 84.88 yen, down 0.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 Others in the market, though, said the Nikkei had simply fallen so much relative to markets overseas that investors saw little reason to sell at this point.\par \par \uc2 The Nikkei is currently down roughly 11 percent since the start of the year, compared to a 2.2 percent rise in the S&P 500 and a 9 percent rise in Seoul shares.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Nikkei lost 35.79 points to 9,566.32, while the broader Topix shed 0.4 percent to 846.52.\par \par \uc2 Resistance was holding near 9,600, the level of the Nikkei's 100-day moving average, despite the benchmark narrowly closing above that level on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "Things in Japan aren't all that good economically, especially in regard to deflation, but shares have been sold quite a lot already and U.S. shares appear to have settled down, both of which will provide support," said Kenichi Hirano, operating officer at Tachibana Securities.\par \par \uc2 "At the same time, there's no reason to buy Japan."\par \par \uc2 Investors had hoped that, with recent improvements in economic data, the Fed would issue a more upbeat outlook or clarify the measures it would take to stimulate demand.\par \par \uc2 But Fed Chairman Ben Bernanke has ratcheted up the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's focus on the threat of deflation that, combined with a grimmer take on the economy hinting at lower growth projections, appeared to clear the way for a new phase of bond buying, or quantitative easing.\par \par \uc2 The Fed also kept overnight interest rates unchanged near zero, as had been expected.\par \par \uc2 PANASONIC CLIMBS\par \par \uc2 Panasonic Corp\uc2  surged 2.4 percent to 1,138 yen after the Nikkei business daily said the company was abandoning the idea of issuing new shares to help finance tender offers currently underway to take total control of two group firms.\par \par \uc2 Instead, Panasonic will use on-hand liquidity and loans to complete the buyouts of \uc2 Sanyo Electric\uc2  and \uc2 Panasonic Electric Works\uc2 , the paper said.\par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 Sharp Corp\uc2  rose 1.3 percent to 857 yen after it announced plans to buy solar power company Recurrent Energy for up to $305 million to expand its footprint in the solar field.\par \par \uc2 But shares of companies with strong exposure to China, such as Komatsu and \uc2 Hitachi Construction Machinery\uc2 , extended losses from the previous day as a row between Japan and China over ownership of islets in the East China Sea dragged on.\par \par \uc2 Komatsu, the world's second-largest maker of earthmoving equipment, fell 2.5 percent to 1,875 yen and Hitachi Construction lost 2.1 percent to 1,815 yen.\par \par \uc2 Trade was thin, with 1.47 billion shares changing hands on the Tokyo exchange's first section, the lowest since Sept 13.\par \par \uc2 Declining shares outnumbered advancing ones, 886 to 575. (Reporting by Elaine Lies; Editing by Joseph Radford)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-JAPAN-STOCKS (UPDATE 5)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100921e69l001hb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
