\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-GLOBAL MARKETS-Stocks, bonds rise on Fed easing view\b0\par\par\uc2 850 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2010\par 16:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Dollar below 85 yen; dealers on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  watch\par \par \uc2 * Government bond yields fall, Fed seen buying debt soon\par \par \uc2 * Gold near a record high hit on Tuesday\par \par \uc2 * Asia stocks up 0.7 pct but Nikkei wavers\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Plumberg\par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Sept 22 (Reuters) - Expectations that the Federal Reserve is moving closer toward printing more money to support the U.S. economy lifted both stocks and bonds on Wednesday, while the dollar fell to a six-week low against the euro on a dwindling yield advantage.\par \par \uc2 Gold was in sight of $1,300 an ounce, having hit a record high overnight after the Fed said it was ready if needed to add more stimulus and that inflation was running below where it would like it to be.\par \par \uc2 Asia ex-Japan stocks rose 0.7 percent to a near two-year high, though trading volumes were thinned out by holidays, while U.S. stock futures climbed 0.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 The increasing possibility that the Fed will buy Treasuries to stimulate demand lifted government bonds, while the prospect of investors having access to even more cheaply borrowed money supported riskier investments such as equities.\par \par \uc2 "The FOMC seems to be considering more bond purchases predominantly because of concerns over deflation and not over growth. In consequence, Asian risky assets should benefit from the additional liquidity rather than suffering from weakening prospects for regional exports to the United States," Dariusz Kowalczyk, senior economist and strategist at Credit Agricole CIB in Hong Kong, said in a note.\par \par \uc2 The falling dollar pushed up the yen and kept traders on high alert for signs that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets again to push its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back down.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets would be "unavoidable" if there was a drastic change in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He also told the Financial Times in an interview that Tokyo planned a "total" package of measures that would boost domestic demand and help to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar fell 0.3 percent against the yen to 84.87 yen just below where traders had thought \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would support it.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last Wednesday to weaken the yen for the first time since 2004, but the dollar has met selling pressure from exporters around 86 yen. Tokyo has not been seen in the market since.\par \par \uc2 DOLLAR OUTLOOK DARKENS\par \par \uc2 The euro rose to $1.3310 the highest since Aug 6, while the dollar weakened across the board.\par \par \uc2 "I doubt the market will step back from selling the U.S. dollar much for the time being until the U.S. data starts to improve," said Greg Gibbs, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2  in Sydney.\par \par \uc2 The relatively high yielding Australian and New Zealand dollars outperformed other liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rising 0.3 percent and 0.4 percent, respectively, with dealers focusing on the widening yield advantage of these countries against U.S. bonds.\par \par \uc2 The 10-year U.S. Treasury future was up 0.3 percent while in the cash market, the benchmark 10-year yield slipped 3 basis points compared with late on Tuesday in New York to 2.55 percent\par \par \uc2 The spread of the U.S. 10-year yield over the German 10-year yield has shrank to a negligible 8 basis points from around 40 basis points only two weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 The Fed's statement increased expectations the Bank of Japan could also ease policy further, pushing up Japanese government bonds. The 10-year JGB future was up 0.3 point in mid session trade.\par \par \uc2 Japan's Nikkei share average was largely unchanged on the day, though it has risen around 9 percent so far in September. Those returns were roughly level with the U.S. S&P 500 index but exceeded the FTSEurofirst 300's 5 percent gain.\par \par \uc2 The MSCI index of Asia Pacific stocks outside Japan was at its highest since April 15. The index has climbed 10 percent in September.\par \par \uc2 However, some Asian exchange-traded funds, which have been receiving heavy inflows, may be near a peak.\par \par \uc2 "We believe inflows are likely to slow, as many of these ETFs are now technically overbought. In addition, we expect ETFs investing in Japan and Taiwan to continue to underperform their Asian peers due to persistent outflows," TrimTabs Investment Research said in a research report.\par \par \uc2 Equity trading volumes in Asia could be light on Wednesday with markets closed in China, South Korea and Taiwan because of public holidays.\par \par \uc2 Gold in the spot market was up 0.1 percent to $1,287.75 per ounce near an all-time high of $1,290.70 reached on Tuesday. The precious metal has been driven by speculation that with advanced economies still more likely essentially to print money, inflation may not be too far off.\par \par \uc2 Crude oil futures drew support from the weaker dollar to edge above $75 a barrel. (Additional reporting by Charlotte Cooper in TOKYO) (Editing by Kim Coghill)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-GLOBAL (WRAPUP 2)|LANGEN|GNN|DNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100921e69l0010m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
