e target at Oct. 5 policy meeting, says Terry McCrann, columnist for the Herald Sun newspaper and a widely watched commentator on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There could also be a back-to-back hike in November, McCrann adds. Says RBA has signaled it has to start raising rates before its sees a rise in inflation, the premptive move driven by the strength of the mining boom. Elsewhere, Alan Mitchell, RBA watcher with the Australian Financial Review says there's more than a slight possibility the RBA will hike in October. Tightening labor markets and an investment booms means the RBA may have to step in to take some steam out of the economy. (james.glynn@dowjones.com) [ 09-20-10 1913ET ]\par \par \uc2 2236 GMT [Dow Jones] AUD/USD remains well supported in dips after rushing to a fresh 2-year high overnight of 0.9494. One senior trader at a U.S. investment bank says option strike bunched around 0.9500 will prove stiff resistance. Adds few participants are likely to want to build fresh long positions ahead of FOMC outcome. But says the last 24 hours have sharply raised expectations RBA will again raise rates before the end of the year, so any falls will be limited for now. RBA board meeting minutes at 0130 GMT will be closely watched, but aren't expected to add much to hawkish picture already well formed in markets. AUD/USD now 0.9458. (james.glynn@dowjones.com) [ 09-20-10 1913ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100920e69k000da\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
