\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  VIEW:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\uc2  Raises Fear Of Competitive Measures\b0\par\par\uc2 By Don Curren and Karen Johnson   \par \uc2 A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN   \par \uc2 791 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2010\par 20:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's incursion into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last week has sparked fears of a wave of competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from other countries, particularly because \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move has met with little rebuke from U.S. officials.\par \par \uc2 Japan's unilateral measure last week to quell strength in the yen calls to mind an era when governments actively sought a trade advantage over their foreign rivals through managed exchange rates.\par \par \uc2 Geoffrey Yu, a \uc2 UBS\uc2  analyst in London wrote "the beggar-thy-neighbour policies which many have feared since the Great Recession began are a step closer to becoming the norm." Yu believes the trend is well established. Two Group of 10 countries that rely on the exports sector--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Switzerland--have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year to hinder their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' appreciation. Colombia \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, and Brazil said it was watching rates carefully.\par \par \uc2 Many major emerging economies manage their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to some degree, he said. In fact, only a handful of countries in the Group of 20 advanced and emerging economies don't manage their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in some way, Yu said.\par \par \uc2 What's changed the game now, at least potentially, is the relatively scant criticism of Japan's move from other key jurisdictions. There have been some scattered complaints, but no resounding condemnation from the Group of Seven.\par \par \uc2 Luxembourg Prime Minister Jean-Claude Juncker, who heads the Eurogroup of finance ministers, did strike out at \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying his euro-zone partners "don't like unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief expressed skepticism that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stem the yen's strength without coordination with other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issuers.\par \par \uc2 "When it comes to Japan, there's no doubt it can't be achieved through a single country's effort," said Bank of Korea Governor Kim Choong-soo.\par \par \uc2 In the U.S., one powerful Democratic U.S. congressman, Sander Levin of Michigan, has called the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "deeply disturbing."\par \par \uc2 But the White House and the Treasury Department have been silent. And that makes all the difference for other countries considering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support their exporters, said \uc2 UBS\uc2 's Yu.\par \par \uc2 "If they see America as giving Japan a free rein, then why not?" he said. "Now that Japan's moved, there are no downsides."\par \par \uc2 Yu ranks Sweden, Australia and New Zealand as potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenors\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Other analysts aren't convinced \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will set a precedent for major economies outside of Asia, where managing exchange rates is a well established practice.\par \par \uc2 "The obvious place for that to show up would be other parts of Asia, and there, central banks have already been quite active in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent months," said \uc2 Adam Cole\uc2 , global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in London. "So, it's almost as if Japan is lagging, rather than leading, the rest of Asia in terms of stepping up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Among other major economies, RBC's estimates suggest there aren't that many obvious \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  misalignments at current levels, Cole said.\par \par \uc2 "Most policymakers are not unhappy with current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate levels. Clearly the Bank of Japan is an exception to that, and the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  is an exception to that," he said.\par \par \uc2 Others say it would take a far greater move in the yen to prompt a widening tide of competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "If the Japanese are going to continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and drive the dollar back up to Y95 or Y100, then maybe--maybe--other countries would be squeezed by the depreciation of the yen," said Marc Chandler, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo markets were closed Monday for a holiday. The dollar was trading Monday afternoon at Y85.76, mostly unchanged from late Friday's level, according to EBS via CQG.\par \par \uc2 At that level, there seems little likelihood the Japanese move will goad any of its major rivals to action soon, Chandler said.\par \par \uc2 "Look, given that the yen is only where it was when I went on vacation in late August, I don't think you should be too worried about it," he said.\par \par \uc2 (Karen Johnson writes about Canadian fixed income and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for Dow Jones Newswires. She can be reached at 416-306-2022; or via email: karen.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments.) [ 09-20-10 1457ET ]\par \par \uc2 1141   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100920e69k000bf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
