\par\par \b \uc2 BOK Governor: Japan's Unilateral Move To Curb Yen Gains Not Effective\b0\par\par\uc2 264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2010\par 05:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL (Dow Jones)--Japan's unilateral action to curb the yen's strength against the dollar won't be as effective as desired and thus requires global coordination, the chief of South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "Japan alone can't solve the problem. The effect of its unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be limited," Bank of Korea Gov. Kim Choong-soo told reporters Friday. His comments were embargoed until Sunday.\par \par \uc2 "The biggest lesson we have learned from the latest global financial crisis is that there should be international economic policy coordination in addressing each country's problems. Market uncertainties can be removed when policymakers send a coordinated signal," he said.\par \par \uc2 He declined to say whether the Korean authorities would also take action with regard to the won versus the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The South Korean won traded at KRW1,160.5 per dollar late Friday in Seoul and some analysts expect the won to strengthen to the KRW1,100 level by the end of this year, driven by strong foreign fund inflows attracted by faster-than-expected domestic economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Last week, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in more than six years, launching a wave of yen-selling totaling an estimated Y2 trillion to counter what it calls "the severe economic conditions" facing the country.\par \par \uc2 Japanese officials have not ruled out further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's gains.\par \par \uc2 -By In-Soo Nam, Dow Jones Newswires; 822-3700-1902; In-Soo.Nam@dowjones.com [ 19-09-10 0300GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100919e69j00009\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
