\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Ex-MOF Utsumi: No Need For  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  To Keep  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 730 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2010\par 03:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 16 Sep 2010 21:49 EDT *DJ  Ex-MOF Utsumi: \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Was 'Effective'; Timing 'Wonderful'\par \par \uc2 16 Sep 2010 21:49 EDT *DJ  Ex-MOF Utsumi: BOJ Ought Not To Sterilize \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 16 Sep 2010 21:49 EDT *DJ  Utsumi: No Chance Of Coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  With Other Countries\par \par \uc2 16 Sep 2010 21:49 EDT *DJ  Ex-MOF Utsumi: MOF Should Always Be Ready To Act Again\par \par \uc2 16 Sep 2010 21:49 EDT *DJ  Ex-MOF Utsumi: Recent Yen Surge Can't Be Justified\par \par \uc2 16 Sep 2010 21:50 EDT DJ  INTERVIEW: No Need For Long \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Program -EX-MOF Utsumi\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Mochizuki \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Japanese government's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this week was highly successful and will not need to be prolonged or expensive, according to a former top Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official who guided \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  campaigns in the past.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was a wake-up call," Makoto Utsumi told Dow Jones Newswires Thursday. "Investors will wonder whether the yen is really a safe \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , so there is no need for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese unit had been strengthening steadily over the past few months. Although returns on yen investments have traditionally been very low, the fallout from the financial crisis has pushed U.S. and European yields to nearly as low levels, narrowing the gap and prompting investors to seek the "safe-haven" of Japan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But Utsumi questioned this argument, saying that Japan's growth momentum is weak, interest rates are ultra-low and outstanding debt is the largest among industrialized nations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's just hard to understand why money is lured to the yen," said Utsumi, who was vice finance minister for international affairs between 1989 and 1991, the key post in guiding the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy. He is now president of the Japan Credit Rating Agency.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan stepped in Wednesday morning with an estimated Y1.8 trillion in yen selling after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose to a fresh 15-year high of Y82.87 to the dollar. The timing took many market participants by surprise, many had anticipated that Tokyo would act only if the dollar fell sharply to the Y80 level.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Utsumi, a 76-year-old former bureaucrat who was involved in massive yen-selling campaigns to fight the surging yen as a result of the Plaza Accord in 1985, said that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is a psychological war against speculators and in that sense, the latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  launch was a "job well done".\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It was such wonderful timing. I think (the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) was very effective," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Utsumi said the finance ministry will not likely need to spend a great deal of money for this campaign in comparison to previous \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . In 2003-2004, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold Y35 trillion yen over a 15-month period to arrest a strong rise in the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But he said that it is important for MOF to remain on standby.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  needs to be always ready to unsheathe its sword," he said, adding that it is a battle that Japan will need to fight on its own.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We're not in a situation where we can get the U.S. and Europe into a coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  because the dollar and the euro are not particularly in trouble at the moment," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Utsumi added that in order to maximize the positive effects of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should not drain the extra funds that result from the market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ has signaled that intention, reporting that its current-account balance--the funds that financial institutions in Japan keep at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which they can use for lending or other needs--will rise to Y17.09 trillion Friday from Thursday's Y15.09 trillion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has pushed the dollar up to a range of Y85, Utsumi said that the current yen levels are not "normal," and the yen should weaken to Y95 to the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He said that at current levels, there is still a risk that companies will continue to relocate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  overseas, putting a further strain on the domestic economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Takashi Mochizuki, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2782; takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 16, 2010 21:50 ET (01:50 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100917e69h000be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
