bashvili@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0835 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CNY turns lower as strong EUR, gains in most regional stocks support risk-sensitive Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  including CNY. On OTC, USD/CNY hits low at 6.7240 vs 6.7322 intraday high, 6.7248 last close; pair last at 6.7248. "The renewed yuan strength is all driven by the euro's move," says Shanghai-based trader at local bank. "I think it's likely the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to set the dollar-yuan central parity at fresh record low next week, though the magnitude of the decline will be small." Next support tipped at 6.7200; "exporters' demand to exchange dollars into yuan in the deliverable forwards market has been decreasing in the past 1-2 months, indicating their orders may not be that strong." (joy.shaw@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0832 GMT [Dow Jones] Safe haven Treasurys are down in London as risk sentiment improves, with equities firm in Europe and the EUR higher across the board. Recent economic data in the US have also tempered worries over a slide back in to recession, easing talk of additional asset purchases by the Fed. Friday's data releases include CPI data at 1230 GMT and the University of Michigan consumer survey at 1355 GMT. The 2-year note is lower at 99-23/32 to yield 0.517%, the 10-year note is down at 98-17/32 to yield 2.795%. The 30-year bond is down at 98-26+/32, yielding 3.941%. December bunds are down 0.19 at 129.20. December gilts are 0.17 lower at 122.17. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0822 GMT [Dow Jones] The EUR is up as risk sentiment improves. Apart from Spain's and France's successful bond auctions on Thursday, the mood is being lifted by the lack of any disappointing economic data and a general rally in global equities. Commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the AUD, are major gainers too, helped by the rise in global liquidity from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the prospect of more QE from the Fed. The JPY is fairly stable against the USD as the market waits to see if the BOJ will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  any more. The USD is up a little at Y85.88 while the EUR is up at $1.3146. The GBP is up at $1.5717 despite disappointing UK data on Thursday. (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0819 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/MYR lower late at 3.1040 vs Wednesday's 3.1160, tracking broad USD weakness vs regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , EUR, says local dealer. Malaysia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  not spotted today but players think \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could buy "at the MYR3.1000 level and that forms a psychological barrier," dealer says. Expects support to stay firm today but MYR likely well bid in near term. Tips 3.1000-3.1200 range for Monday. (kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com) [ 09-17-10 0455ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100917e69h00062\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
