\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:EUR/USD,EUR/JPY Ride Positive Stocks Higher-Dealer\b0\par\par\uc2 1,422 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2010\par 06:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0424 GMT [Dow Jones] Risk-sensitive EUR rises vs USD, JPY as strong regional share markets prompt short-term investors to buy; if equities in Europe, New York also gain, EUR/USD could rise to 1.3200, EUR/JPY to 113.00 by end of global day, says senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealer at major Japan bank. "It's a 'risk-on' market today, and that's helping the euro and yen crosses, while weighing on the dollar," dealer says. EUR/USD last 1.3105, EUR/JPY 112.38. AUD/JPY up at last 80.75 vs earlier low at 80.18. NZD/JPY at 62.52 vs earlier low 62.07. (andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0423 GMT [Dow Jones] India government bonds down amid remaining negative sentiment after RBI's aggressive rate tightening Thursday, tight liquidity, says dealer with state-run bank; 7.80% 2020 benchmark bond at 98.81 vs 98.90 Thursday's close. "Being the last session before the weekend, traders may avoid taking new positions. The markets now keenly await the government's borrowing calendar for October-March," due by end-September, says dealer. Expects borrowing in 2H to be as stated in March, (INR1.7 trillion) if not lower. Tips 10-year yields in 7.95%-8.00% range in session. (nupur.acharya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0417 GMT [Dow Jones] HSI +1.1% at 21,932.13, with index approaching 22,000 (early high at 21,973.08, after China markets turn positive (Shanghai Composite +0.3%), while sentiment in markets also supported in part by expectations of more CNY appreciation ahead after PBOC sets USD/CNY central parity at new record low of 6.7172, says Prudential's associate director Alvin Cheung. "This is expected to help support those companies which are sensitive to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moves. I would suggest buying more commodity and airline stocks on dips as they are set to benefit from this trend." Among commodities, Chalco (2600.HK) +2.1% at HK$6.81, Cnooc (0883.HK) +1.2% at HK$14.78 while for airlines, \uc2 Air China\uc2  (0753.HK) +2.3% at HK$9.44, \uc2 China Eastern\uc2  (0670.HK) +0.7% at HK$4.38. (susanna.tai@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0413 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares end +1.8% at 457.58 on expectations \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will allow banks to give more low-cost loans from October to support companies in 4Q. "Sentiment is also rising on 3Q earnings hopes after some bluechip firms posted strong results for August," says trader. Volume moderate with 50 million shares valued at VND1.28 trillion exchanging hands. Among most actives, Ocean Group (OGC.VH) ends +4.9% at VND36,700, Saigon Securities (SSI.VH) +4.8% at VND28,400, REE (REE.VH) +4.2% at VND17,300. Traders tip index to test 480 resistance next week. (phammuoi.nguyen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0412 GMT [Dow Jones] China shares turn higher midday in light trade, led by electric power generation companies after \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  analyst Pierre Lau said in note Thursday NDRC recommended raising electricity prices in 7 provinces. Shanghai Composite Index +0.3% at 2609.17, tipped to trade in tight range around 2600 for rest of session. Banks still mixed; "we're seeing very light trading in banks and overall volume is too low for the index to stage a strong rebound," says Han Hao at China Minzu Securities; notes, Agricultural Bank of China (601288.SH) down 1.5% at CNY2.59, extending losses for fourth consecutive session, further denting sentiment on sector. \uc2 Huaneng Power International\uc2  (600011.SH) last +5.1% at CNY6.36, \uc2 Huadian Power International\uc2  (600027.SH) +3.4% at CNY3.97, ICBC (601398.SH) flat at CNY3.97. Trade volume CNY51.0 billion at midday, less than 40% of previous session's volume at close. Shenzhen Composite Index +0.4% at 1160.99. (jean.yung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0406 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan's new 10-year government bond down on debut, yield last at 1.2415% vs yesterday's auction yield of 1.2278%; trader from local brokerage says investors not snapping up more long-duration paper on back of gains in stock market. "I didn't see much interest in the market to buy more (of the 10-year paper) this morning." Tips 10-year yield in 1.22%-1.28% band next week. 5-year government bond yield last at 0.88% vs 0.86% late yesterday, tipped in 0.87%-0.93% range next week. Taiex last +1.1% at 8190.43. (aries.poon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0404 GMT [Dow Jones] Sensex +0.9% at 19,591.05 on gains in offshore markets, fund buying by institutions; 29 of 30 index issues higher with heavyweight Larsen (500510.BY) +1.3% at INR1,958.50, RIL (500325.BY) +0.9% at INR1,009.50, Bharti (532454.BY) +2.3% at INR355.85. "The opening is far better than expected. Liquidity is driving stocks while some short-covering, mainly in technology stocks after falling yesterday, has helped," says dealer at local brokerage. Puts resistance at 19,660 though adds some consolidation could set in before weekend. DLF (532868.BY) +1.6% at INR355.50, TCS (532540.BY) +1.6% at INR909.55, Wipro (507685.BY) +1.4% at INR429.25. (gurdev.singh@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0403 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR down as higher India shares, stronger EUR support INR, says dealer with private bank; pair at 46.05 vs 46.15 late yesterday. Dealer says it may test 46.00 with 46.00-46.15 range for day; adds if 46.00 gives way convincingly, pair may touch 45.90. Another dealer with state-run bank says 46.04-46.05 level may be attractive for oil importers to buy.(nupur.acharya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0357 GMT [Dow Jones] Citi expects one or possibly two more rates hikes in next 6 months, while will raise repo, reverse repo by 50 basis points each. Notes, while "there is a change in tone to more positive" as RBI has said that tightening done so far "has taken the monetary situation close to normal", inflation remains significantly above trends. "Interest rates hikes into the latter half of 2011 will be dependent on how both the domestic and global macro pans out," says house. Notes, given current trends in liquidity and uncertainty on bond auction calendar, 10-year yields could remain under pressure and likely trade in 7.90% to 8.05% range (currently 7.98%). (subhadip.sircar@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0355 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY may rise to 86.00 as short-term speculators begin piling into USD/JPY long positions in expectation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken JPY further, says senior dealer at major \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  bank. "Speculative moves are coming back," this time, includes players going long dollar, dealer says. Additional gains unlikely, however, as Japan exporters will likely intensify USD sales as end-of-quarter approaches. Says pair may trade in 85.20-86.00 range if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities don't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in global day. Pair last 85.76. (kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0346 GMT [Dow Jones] Nomura Securities says RBI likely to pause rest of FY, given expectation growth and inflation will moderate; "inflation has already started tapering off, and we expect a further decline in the coming months as input cost pressures ease." Unless commodity prices spike and put upward pressure on inflation, further rate hikes are unlikely this FY. Says RBI has signaled a shift in policy stance from "normalising mode to a data-dependent/neutral mode." (subhadip.sircar@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0345 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Westpac\uc2  sells unit of NZD/USD at 0.7280, targeting 0.7000 stop loss around 0.7400 after RBNZ's bearish outlook, says strategist Robert Rennie. Says NZD has stayed high despite weakening fundamentals, but that should change. "We believe the RBNZ yesterday has forced a resolution of this divergence, by significantly downgrading its interest rate track for the current tightening cycle. NZ-U.S. interest rate differentials have narrowed further, and this should eventually take its toll on NZD/USD." NZD/USD last at 0.7280 (enda.curran@dowjones.com) [ 09-17-10 0024ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100917e69h0002t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
