\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/KRW A Tad Lower; Good Support Put At 1,160\b0\par\par\uc2 1,708 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2010\par 02:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0020 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/KRW slips to 1,163.4 vs 1,164.5 late yesterday amid Kospi's mild 0.3% gain; traders put firm support at 1,160, expect quiet session before Chuseok holiday Sept. 21-Sept. 23. In longer term, KRW likely to rise on back of country's economic recovery but "just for day trading, players could have a go at making dollar-long bets" on any USD dips, says local bank trader. (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0015 GMT [Dow Jones] After surging earlier this week on Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's major auto and electronics shares higher today with USD/JPY remaining solid (now 85.80); still stocks' rally may be limited today, says Tachibana Securities operating officer Kenichi Hirano. Sentiment would be more bullish had USD/JPY risen further (above 86), but with yen-weakening momentum slowing, traders likely to sit tight for now, he says. "There are no domestic trading cues, and it's kind of bad timing with a major holiday week coming up." Japanese market closed next Monday and Thursday for national holidays. \uc2 Sony\uc2  (6758.TO) up 0.6% at Y2,658. Canon (7751.TO) up 0.3% at Y3,865. Nintendo (7974.OK) up 0.5% at Y23,870. \uc2 Toyota Motor\uc2  (7203.TO) up 0.5% at Y3,075, \uc2 Honda Motor\uc2  (7267.TO) up 1.4% at Y3,000. (juro.osawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0014 GMT [Dow Jones] Lead December JGB futures tad down as Tokyo shares higher (Nikkei now up 0.8%), may extend declines to 142.07, say