\par\par \b \uc2 Q+A-What is  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  capacity for  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2 ?\b0\par\par\uc2 By Yoko Nishikawa   \par \uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2010\par 14:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets this week for the first time in more than six years, selling as much as 1.86 trillion yen ($21.7 billion) to pull the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back from a 15-year high against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The estimate is based on Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market data and if correct means the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday was a record amount for a single day of official yen selling.\par \par \uc2 The last time \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , authorities sold 35 trillion yen over a 15-month period up to March 2004.\par \par \uc2 Below are some questions and answers about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's capacity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market:\par \par \uc2 HOW DOES \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2  FINANCE \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 By law, the government has no right to print cash and has to fund its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by issuing financing bills (FBs), usually of three-month duration. It sets the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amount and the BOJ, which has the right to print cash, acts as its agent.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is managed through a special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  budget account that is reviewed each year by parliament as part of the regular compilation of the budget.\par \par \uc2 HOW MUCH MONEY IS IN \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 'S \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  WAR CHEST?\par \par \uc2 The special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  budget account currently limits borrowing for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 145 trillion yen. Tokyo boosted the ceiling this fiscal year by 5 trillion yen, the first increase in six years, sparking market speculation the government was signalling its willingness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, more than 100 trillion yen of the borrowing is used to fund the existing foreign reserves.\par \par \uc2 So after Wednesday's selling, the available ammunition for fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is about 34 or 36 trillion yen, roughly the same level as the 35 trillion yen \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  used for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between January 2003 and March 2004.\par \par \uc2 ARE THERE OTHER OPTIONS FOR FINANCING \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 The ceiling is not set in stone. The MOF could raise the ceiling in a special budget request, a step it took in the midst of 2003-2004 yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, that would require parliamentary approval.\par \par \uc2 In addition, some in the MOF are already concerned that steadily rising issuance of short-term bills could distort supply and demand in the debt market, making authorities more cautious about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The MOF could also sell foreign assets to the Bank of Japan. In 2003, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreed to lend up to 10 trillion yen to the MOF in exchange for U.S. Treasuries under repurchase agreements. ($1=85.75 Yen) (Editing by Edmund Klamann and Neil Fullick)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Q+A)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100917e69h000u1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
