\par\par \b \uc2 MONEY MARKETS-US repo rates ease; no sign of Japan buying\b0\par\par\uc2 667 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2010\par 10:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Repo rates ease further in the wake of supply settlement\par \par \uc2 * No evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying T-bills since \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Interbank euro rates seen edging up as loans come due (Updates U.S. action, changes dateline, previous London)\par \par \uc2 By Richard Leong and Emelia Sithole-Matarise\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK/LONDON, Sept 17 (Reuters) - Overnight rates in the U.S. government debt repurchase market slipped on Friday as demand from bond dealers to finance last week's $67 billion in coupon-bearing Treasury supply faded.\par \par \uc2 Overnight rates on repurchases or repos were last bid at 0.31 percent, down from 0.36 percent on Thursday. It was bid as high as 0.38 percent <USONRP=> earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 In a repo, a dealer uses a Treasury security as collateral to raise cash and pledges to buy it back the next day.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, there has been no sign that Japan has scooped up Treasury bills in a significant way, since the second-biggest holder of U.S. government debt weakened the yen on Wednesday to try to boost exports.\par \par \uc2 "We haven't seen any footprint from the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Alex Roever, short-term fixed-income strategist with \uc2 J.P. Morgan Securities\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 The rate on three-month Treasury bills <US3MT=RR> last traded at 0.15 percent late Friday, little changed from Tuesday's close prior to the yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Six years ago when \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last engaged in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  it had frequently bought T-bills, together with longer-dated government debt, Roever said.\par \par \uc2 According to Federal Reserve data released Thursday, foreign central banks' holding of Treasuries jumped to $2.444 trillion, up $39.6 billion from a week ago. For more see [ID:nNLLGKE6GO].\par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have totaled 1.8 trillion yen ($20.98 billion). [ID:nTKW007123]\par \par \uc2 It is unclear whether the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reinvested any of its dollar purchases into Treasuries, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 The BoJ said on Wednesday it is ready to leave its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilized, a phrasing that signals it is not buying Treasuries. [ID:nTKX006996]\par \par \uc2 While T-bill rates have held steady since Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  move, long-dated U.S. government debt yields have swung wildly as traders have been betting as to whether Japan will plow its dollars into Treasuries, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "The question is whether it becomes a pattern," Roever said of future BoJ yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 EURO FUND RATES STEADY\par \par \uc2 Across the Atlantic, interbank euro funding rates were steady to slightly lower, but they could grind higher in coming weeks as banks prepare to pay back 225 billion euros in maturing loans to the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Although the ECB has pledged to extend unlimited financing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  into next year, the level of short-dated rates will depend on how much of the maturing debt banks roll over into shorter-dated loans on Sept. 30.\par \par \uc2 "We would expect a good chunk of the maturing 225 billion euros to be rolled down into the 1-week MROs. Lenders still appear thin on the ground and any return of demand to the open market would most likely exert significant upward pressure on rates," said Chris Clark, an analyst at ICAP in London.\par \par \uc2 Three-month EONIA <EONIA=> rates have risen to 53.9 basis points from 50.1 late last Friday while six-month EONIA has climbed to 60.8 from 55.9, according to ICAP data.\par \par \uc2 However, three-month benchmark Euribor rates <EURIBOR3MD=> -- traditionally the main gauge of unsecured interbank euro lending and a mix of interest rate expectations and banks' appetite for lending -- held steady at 0.879 percent on still ample excess liquidity in the system.\par \par \uc2 London interbank offered rates for three-month euros were fixed slightly lower at 0.82875 percent <EUR3MFSR=>, down from 0.83000 percent on Thursday. [ID:nEAP000025]. (Editing by James Dalgleish)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-MONEY (WRAPUP 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|U|UKI|J|RNP|DNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100917e69h000ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
