\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For September 17\b0\par\par\uc2 1,757 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2010\par 09:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN PM ANNOUNCES NEW CABINET; KEEPS NODA AS FINANCE MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan tweaked his Cabinet Friday, replacing his economy, trade and foreign ministers but retaining Yoshihiko Noda as finance minister, ensuring continuity in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy as Tokyo fights a strong yen that threatens the economy. (published 0548 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER VOWS TO ACT VS YEN AGAIN IF NEEDED \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister threatened Friday to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market again if necessary to weaken the yen, signaling the government's resolve to defend the nation's export-led economy despite criticism from abroad. (published 0345 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: PBOC SEES RISKS INCLUDING INFLATION, FINANCIAL SECTOR WOES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Though economic confidence is increasing, China still faces many challenges in maintaining a fast and stable growth rate, including inflation risks and possible problems in the financial sector, the People's Bank of China said Friday. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC OFFICIAL COMMENTS ON YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , SAYS STRONGER DOLLAR WOULD BE GOOD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. dollar appreciation would be good, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Zhang Jianhua\f28 \uc2 \f2 , head of the People's Bank of China's research bureau, said Friday in response to a question about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to suppress the value of the yen. (published 0459 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA REGULATOR: TOUGHER CAPITAL REQUIREMENTS NEEDED FOR BIG BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's large banks need tougher capital requirements than their smaller rivals, a senior official with the country's banking regulator said Friday, in the latest sign of growing official concerns about the potential risks in the country's financial system as Beijing unwinds its massive economic stimulus program. (published 0451 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA YUAN ENDS 6-DAY RALLY VS DOLLAR AFTER GEITHNER TESTIMONY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan ended its six-day rally against the U.S. dollar on Friday, following a less aggressive effort by China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to guide its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher after the completion of the closely watched U.S. Congressional hearings on Beijing's exchange-rate policy. (published 0530 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ EXPECTS CURRENT ACCOUNT BALANCE AT Y17.10 TLN FRI VS Y15.09 TLN THU \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan's latest forecast showed it expects its current account balance to increase by Y2 trillion Friday, indicating that it doesn't plan, at least for now, to soak up the yen that the government sold Wednesday in its massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 2317 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: IMF: BANK INDONESIA'S MONETARY POLICY APPROPRIATE FOR NOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia's current monetary policy stance is appropriate given that inflation is within the target range and the risk that hiking rates now could attract more volatile portfolio capital, the International Monetary Fund said Friday. (published 0428 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PROPOSES MEASURES TO STEM BAHT RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand is considering five measures proposed by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  to help curb the baht's strength, Finance Minister Korn Chatikavanij said Friday. (published 0622 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: SINGAPORE AUGUST NON-OIL EXPORTS UP 31.2% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's key non-oil exports rose at a faster-than-expected pace in August, rising 31.2% from a year earlier due to robust gains in the electronics and the pharmaceuticals sectors. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: NZ 3Q CONSUMER CONFIDENCE SLIPS BUT REMAINS RESILIENT - WESTPAC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\f28 \uc2 \f2 -McDermott Miller Consumer Confidence Index fell to 114.1 points in the third quarter from 119.3 points in the second quarter as the economic recovery remains patchy, a survey published Friday showed. (published 2316 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC CHANGES MONETARY POLICY COMMITTEE MEMBERS; ADDS ICBC CHAIRMAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China on Friday announced changes to the members of the People's Bank of China monetary policy committee, a consultative body that advises the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on monetary policy decisions. (published 0425 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG ELECTRONICS\f28 \uc2 \f2  CEO NAM YONG RESIGNS; SHARES SOAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LG Electronics Co. Chief Executive Nam Yong resigned Friday amid the company's difficulties reshaping its cellphone business for smartphones. (published 0303 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  CHINA EVERBRIGHT BANK RAISES CNY21.7 BLN IN IPO AFTER GREENSHOE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Everbright Bank Co. raised a total of CNY21.7 billion from its Shanghai listing after fully exercising the initial public offering's over-allotment option. (published 0021 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA SUNTIEN HK IPO AIMS TO RAISE ABOUT US$440 MLN - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Clean energy producer China Suntien Green Energy Corp. plans to raise about US$440 million in an initial public offering ahead of a Hong Kong listing Oct. 13, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Friday. (published 0445 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CEBU PACIFIC STARTS IPO ROADSHOW SEPT 24; PRICE SETTING OCT 8 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cebu Air Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., better known as Cebu Pacific, will begin on Sept. 24 a roadshow for its long-delayed initial public offer that the Philippines' largest budget carrier by sales expects to raise as much as PHP32.19 billion. (published 0101 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SM DEVELOPMENT MAY RAISE UP TO PHP10.5 BLN FROM RIGHTS OFFER -BOURSE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SM Development Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has set an indicative price of PHP5.45 to PHP5.73 for each of the 1.83 billion shares it plans to sell in a stock rights offer, potentially raising as much as PHP10.5 billion for the Philippine property developer, the stock exchange said Friday. (published 0122 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MURCHISON METALS FY10 LOSS A$21.6M V A$18.3M LAST YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Western Australian iron ore explorer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Murchison Metals Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it lost A$21.6 million after tax in the year ended June 30, 2010, as ramp-up expenses continued in the absence of production revenues. (published 0156 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: INDOFOOD CBP, HARUM ENERGY SET IPO PRICES - BANKERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Two Indonesian companies have each set the price for their respective initial public offering of shares, which will both raise a combined IDR8.9 trillion in proceeds. (published 0635 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW: SUNVIC CHEMICAL EYES RECORD ANNUAL PROFIT AS SALES PRICES GROW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SunVic Chemical Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is on track for a record profit in 2010 on the back of higher selling prices, and earnings growth is set to remain robust in coming years helped by cost savings. (published 0117 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ORIENT GREEN POWER SETS IPO IN INR47-INR55 INDICATIVE PRICE BAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's Orient Green Power Ltd. Friday set its proposed INR9 billion initial public offering in the INR47-INR55 indicative price band, it said in a newspaper advertisement. (published 0349 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: HINDUSTAN PETROLEUM PLANS INR9B RETAIL BOOST, NEW REFINERY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hindustan Petroleum Corp. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to invest INR9 billion in its retail \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this fiscal year and set up a new 15 million ton refinery, as it works to grow its downstream businesses. (published 0416 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TELSTRA EXPECTS GROSS PROCEEDS OF ABOUT US$433M FROM SOUFUN IPO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Telstra Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it expects gross proceeds of around US$433 million from the initial public offering of Chinese advertising website \f28 \uc2 \f2 SouFun Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., which is planning to list on the New York Stock Exchange. (published 0525 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ACS TAKEOVER OF LEIGHTON UNLIKELY; STRATEGY MAY CHANGE -ANALYSTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A proposed takeover of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Leighton Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s German parent \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hochtief AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  by Spain's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Actividades de Construccion y Servicios S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 . isn't likely to trigger a full takeover of the Australian construction company but could mean a change of strategy, analysts said Friday. (published 0541 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =RELIANCE MEDIAWORKS TO OPEN 60 SCREENS IN INDIA, 20 IN US THIS FY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cinema chain operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reliance MediaWorks Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is planning to open another 60 screens in India this fiscal year as it aims to tap the fast-growing local movie market, a senior executive said. (published 0514 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TRANSURBAN: WESTLINK M7 RAISES A$505M TO REFINANCE TRANCHE OF MATURING DEBT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Transurban Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday that its half-owned Westlink M7 has refinanced A$505 million to replace a tranche of its debt due to mature in December. (published 0512 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW: RELIANCE MEDIAWORKS TO OPEN 60 SCREENS IN INDIA THIS FY, 20 IN US \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cinema chain operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reliance MediaWorks Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is planning to open another 60 screens in India and 20 in the U.S. this fiscal year through March 2011, a senior executive said. (published 0636 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES UP BUT TRADE QUIET; THAI TELCOS TUMBLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly higher Friday after a mild rise on Wall Street, though investors in Korea and Japan were a little cautious before holidays next week. (published 0354 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA MINISTER HOPES TO HAVE MINING TAX CERTAINTY SOON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Energy Minister Martin Ferguson said Friday he hopes to provide industry certainty on a proposed new levy on mining company profits "sooner rather than later", noting that both investment and government revenue streams are riding on the controversial tax proposal. (published 0321 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA FARM MINISTER: NO PLAN TO LIFT BAN ON WHEAT EXPORTS IMMEDIATELY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India doesn't plan to lift a three-year-old ban on the export of wheat immediately, despite sitting on a huge stockpile of grains, Farm Minister Sharad Pawar said Friday. (published 0638 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: GLOBAL WHEAT SUPPLIERS STUCK WITH LARGE VOLUMES IN UKRAINE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Global suppliers are unable to dispose of several hundred thousand metric tons of wheat they purchased from growers in the Ukraine ahead of harvest in June due to an indefinite delay in shipments, trading executives said Friday. (published 0313 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: XSTRATA,TEPCO AGREE TO OCT-SEP COAL PRICE FLAT WITH APRIL-MARCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 17-09-10 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Swiss-based resources company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xstrata PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has agreed to sell Australian coal to a Japanese utility for the October-September period at $97.75 a metric ton, unchanged from the price it negotiated for April-March, a person familiar with the deal said Friday. (published 0349 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHEVRON, \f28 \uc2 \f2 SINOPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  MAY SIGN SHALE GAS DEAL THIS YEAR -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chevron Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Petrochemical Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or Sinopec Group, will likely sign an agreement by the end of the year to explore and develop jointly shale gas in southwestern China, a person familiar with the matter said Thursday. (published 2351 GMT Thursday)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA TO GET 17 BLN CUBIC METERS GAS VIA CENTRAL ASIA PIPELINE IN 2011 -CNPC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China National Petroleum Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to get 17 billion cubic metres of natural gas transmitted to China through the Central Asia gas pipeline next year, CNPC said in its inhouse newsletter Friday. (published 0344 GMT) [ 17-09-10 0705GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100917e69h000gp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
