\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,026 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2010\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN PM ANNOUNCES NEW CABINET; KEEPS NODA AS FINANCE MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan tweaked his Cabinet Friday, replacing his economy, trade and foreign ministers but retaining Yoshihiko Noda as finance minister, ensuring continuity in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy as Tokyo fights a strong yen that threatens the economy. (published 0548 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER VOWS TO ACT VS YEN AGAIN IF NEEDED \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister threatened Friday to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market again if necessary to weaken the yen, signaling the government's resolve to defend the nation's export-led economy despite criticism from abroad. (published 0345 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: PBOC SEES RISKS INCLUDING INFLATION, FINANCIAL SECTOR WOES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Though economic confidence is increasing, China still faces many challenges in maintaining a fast and stable growth rate, including inflation risks and possible problems in the financial sector, the People's Bank of China said Friday. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC OFFICIAL COMMENTS ON YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , SAYS STRONGER DOLLAR WOULD BE GOOD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. dollar appreciation would be good, Zhang Jianhua, head of the People's Bank of China's research bureau, said Friday in response to a question about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to suppress the value of the yen. (published 0459 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA REGULATOR: TOUGHER CAPITAL REQUIREMENTS NEEDED FOR BIG BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's large banks need tougher capital requirements than their smaller rivals, a senior official with the country's banking regulator said Friday, in the latest sign of growing official concerns about the potential risks in the country's financial system as Beijing unwinds its massive economic stimulus program. (published 0451 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA YUAN ENDS 6-DAY RALLY VS DOLLAR AFTER GEITHNER TESTIMONY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan ended its six-day rally against the U.S. dollar on Friday, following a less aggressive effort by China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to guide its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher after the completion of the closely watched U.S. Congressional hearings on Beijing's exchange-rate policy. (published 0530 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ EXPECTS CURRENT ACCOUNT BALANCE AT Y17.10 TLN FRI VS Y15.09 TLN THU \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan's latest forecast showed it expects its current account balance to increase by Y2 trillion Friday, indicating that it doesn't plan, at least for now, to soak up the yen that the government sold Wednesday in its massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 2317 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PM KAN SET TO ORDER DRAFTING EXTRA BUDGET FOR FISCAL STIMULUS -KYODO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan will order government officials to draft an extra budget for fiscal 2010 to finance an additional stimulus package worth several trillion yen, Kyodo News reported Friday, citing sources close to the matter. (published 0324 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BROKERAGES EXPECT BOJ DI FOR MAKERS TO KEEP RISING IN JULY-SEPT -NIKKEI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brokerages predict that business sentiment among major manufacturers will improve for the sixth straight quarter in the three months through September, the Nikkei reports. (published 0548 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN GOVERNMENT DEBT SURPASSES THAT OF PRIVATE FIRMS IN APRIL-JUNE -NIKKEI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government's outstanding liabilities exceeded those of private companies in the April-June quarter, according to preliminary data the Bank of Japan released Friday. (published 0346 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: IMF: BANK INDONESIA'S MONETARY POLICY APPROPRIATE FOR NOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia's current monetary policy stance is appropriate given that inflation is within the target range and the risk that hiking rates now could attract more volatile portfolio capital, the International Monetary Fund said Friday. (published 0428 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI FINANCE MINISTER: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PROPOSES 5 MEASURES TO STEM BAHT RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand is considering three out of five measures proposed by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  to help curb the baht's strength, Finance Minister Korn Chatikavanij said Friday. (published 0526 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: SINGAPORE AUGUST NON-OIL EXPORTS UP 31.2% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's key non-oil exports rose at a faster-than-expected pace in August, rising 31.2% from a year earlier due to robust gains in the electronics and the pharmaceuticals sectors. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: NZ 3Q CONSUMER CONFIDENCE SLIPS BUT REMAINS RESILIENT - WESTPAC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\f28 \uc2 \f2 -McDermott Miller Consumer Confidence Index fell to 114.1 points in the third quarter from 119.3 points in the second quarter as the economic recovery remains patchy, a survey published Friday showed. (published 2316 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA MINISTER HOPES TO HAVE MINING TAX CERTAINTY SOON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Energy Minister Martin Ferguson said Friday he hopes to provide industry certainty on a proposed new levy on mining company profits "sooner rather than later", noting that both investment and government revenue streams are riding on the controversial tax proposal. (published 0321 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC CHANGES MONETARY POLICY COMMITTEE MEMBERS; ADDS ICBC CHAIRMAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China on Friday announced changes to the members of the People's Bank of China monetary policy committee, a consultative body that advises the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on monetary policy decisions. (published 0425 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA MAY LET LOCAL FIRMS INVEST OFFSHORE YUAN DOMESTICALLY - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China could soon launch a trial to allow domestic financial institutions with yuan-denominated funds in Hong Kong to invest in China's A-share and bond markets, the state-run Securities Times reported Friday, citing unnamed sources. (published 0346 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BBMG: TO ISSUE CNY2 BLN WORTH OF 5-YEAR NOTES IN CHINA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cement company \f28 \uc2 \f2 BBMG Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday it will issue CNY2 billion worth of five-year notes in China, in the first tranche of a CNY2.8 billion medium-term note issuance. (published 0011 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par INTERVIEW: NO NEED FOR LONG \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PROGRAM - EX-MOF UTSUMI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this week was highly successful and will not need to be prolonged or expensive, according to a former top Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official who guided \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  campaigns in the past. (published 0150 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =POINT OF VIEW: NO GOOD ANSWERS IN THE YUAN DEBATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the U.S. Treasury Secretary, there are probably no fun days and less fun days. Maybe history will look more kindly, but it's tough sledding right now. (published 0003 GMT) [ 17-09-10 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100917e69h000by\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
