\par\par \b \uc2 INDIAN MORNING BRIEFING: Sensex Likely To be Rangebound\b0\par\par\uc2 1,672 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2010\par 05:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 DJCS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLOBAL MARKETS \par DJIA                10594.83  +22.10   +0.21% \par Nasdaq              2303.25   +1.93    +0.08% \par S&P 500             1124.66   -0.41    -0.04% \par FTSE 100            5540.14   -15.42   -0.28% \par Nikkei Stock        9580.56   +71.06   +0.75% \par Hang Seng           21792.84  +101.39  +0.47% \par Kospi               1813.92   +2.07    +0.11% \par SGX Nifty           5858.00   +11.00   +0.18% \par Sept. contract \par  \par USD/JPY             85.90-91     +0.23% \par Range               85.93-85.23 \par EUR/USD             1.3077-79    +0.53% \par Range               1.3117-1.2977 \par  \par CBOT Wheat Dec.     $7.192 per bushel \par Comex Gold          $1,273.80    +$5.10 \par Comex Gold Range    $1,266.10-$1,279.50 \par Nymex Crude (NY)    $74.57       -$1.45 \par  \par  \par CHARTING THE SENSEX \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bombay Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 's 30-share Sensitive Index is likely to trade in a 19,340-19,520 range, according to charts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Though the Sensex has been in a steady uptrend for the past eight days, the price action Thursday was marked by volatility. The completion of a "shooting star" candlestick pattern Thursday is a sign of profit-taking and nervousness among market participants.\par \par \uc2 A fall below 19,340 would indicate that a short-term downward corrective phase is underway, and may also lead to a test of major support at 19,050.\par \par \uc2 The National Stock Exchange's 50-share Nifty could be confined to a 5,790-5,840 band.\par \par \uc2 The completion of a bearish "key reversal day" pattern Thursday is a cause of concern. A drop below 5,790 could trigger a fall to major support at 5,750.\par \par \uc2 The Nifty has move past Thursday's intra-day high of 5,901.70 to impart momentum to the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Technology companies boosted U.S. blue-chip stocks to a narrow gain Thursday, as confidence mounted that the economy would avoid a double-dip recession.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Technology stocks led the climb, as investors gained faith that the economic recovery is slowing but not headed toward a second slump. Leading the Dow Industrials' climb, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hewlett-Packard\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose 1.8%, Cisco Systems gained 1.6% and Intel added 1.3%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It seems like we priced in too much of a double dip, and it's not coming to pass as bad as people anticipated," said Patrick Becker, Jr., principal at Becker Capital Management.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Technology just got walloped, and many of the value-oriented tech names really underperformed in the first half of the year," Becker said. "You do have a valuation bounce occurring in those names."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, recent muddy economic data have left investors hesitant about the rally's sustainability and kept trading confined to a narrow range. As concerns over the economy have loosened their grip, anxiety rose Thursday over U.S. lawmakers' aggressive stance on China's exchange-rate policy and the potential to strain relations with China.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ASIAN STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were higher Friday after a mild rise on Wall Street, though investors in South Korea and Japan were a little cautious before holidays next week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Nikkei Share Average, Australia's S&P/ASX 200, South Korea's Kospi Composite and New Zealand's NZX-50 were all up.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Industrial Average futures were 14 points higher in screen trade, helped by after-hours gains for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Oracle\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Research in Motion\f28 \uc2 \f2  as both technology firms posted strong earnings.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese exporters continued to rise as the U.S. dollar remained well supported around 85.80 yen after Tokyo's market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier this week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gains were broad-based with 31 of the 33 Topix subindexes higher, though investors were not trading actively before Japanese public holidays on Monday and Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sony\f28 \uc2 \f2  was up 0.6%, Canon rose 0.3%, Nintendo gained 0.5% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Honda Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2  added 1.4%. GS Yuasa was up 4.2% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . rose 0.8% on a Nikkei report of a joint battery venture in Europe with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Magna International\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Kospi was also in an narrow range before Korean market holidays from Sept. 21 to 23.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Technology stocks were leading the market higher as they tracked their U.S. peers. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics\f28 \uc2 \f2  was up 0.5%, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hynix Semiconductor\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose 2.6% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG Innotek\f28 \uc2 \f2  was 4.9% higher.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  majors kept to tight ranges with all eyes still on the yen and the market on watch for any further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Japanese authorities to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar was at Y85.80, compared with Y85.81 late in New York, while the euro was at $1.3066 from $1.3085 and Y112.11, from Y112.29.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par METALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold futures posted a new record settlement Thursday as the U.S. dollar weakened and investors looked for more of the precious metal as a haven while equities eased.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spot gold was at $1,274.30 per troy ounce, down $1.20 from New York, after touching a record high of $1,277.85 Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Base metals on the London Metal Exchange mostly closed marginally higher Thursday after drifting in recent ranges for much of the session, with mixed U.S. data failing to provide clear direction.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par OIL SUMMARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October Nymex crude oil futures were down 4 cents at $74.53 per barrel on Globex.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CALENDAR OF EVENTS Sept. 17 \par 0900 IST Mumbai:      \f28 \uc2 \f2 Essar Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  executive at event \par 1030 IST New Delhi:   \f28 \uc2 \f2 DLF Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  executive director, Unitech president, \par                       Sunil Mantri Realty chairman at Federation of \par                       Indian Chambers of Commerce and Industry \par                       international real estate summit \par 1100 IST New Delhi:   \f28 \uc2 \f2 Infosys\f28 \uc2 \f2  director, Mahindra Satyam chief \par                       marketing officer, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nokia India\f28 \uc2 \f2  vice president, \par                       Maruti Suzuki executive, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indian Oil\f28 \uc2 \f2  executive \par                       director at event \par 1130 IST Bangalore:   United Breweries chief financial officer, Wipro \par                       executive director at Confederation of Indian \par                       Industry event \par 1145 IST Mumbai:      \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cantabil Retail India\f28 \uc2 \f2  initial public offering \par                       press meet \par 1200 IST New Delhi:   NTPC chairman at press meet \par 1230 IST Mumbai:      Orient Green Power initial public offering press \par                       meet \par 1445 IST Mumbai:      Standard Chartered Asia chief executive at launch \par                       of 'women on corporate boards India 2010' report \par 1530 IST New Delhi:   Finance ministry chief economic adviser at press \par                       meet \par 1530 IST New Delhi:   Finance minister, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  Deputy \par                       Governor Subir Gokarn at ICRIER International \par                       conference \par 1700 IST Mumbai:      Godrej Group chairman, Reliance Capital chief \par                       investment strategist at event \par 1700 IST New Delhi:   \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tata Motors\f28 \uc2 \f2  India managing director at event \par 0800 GMT EU:          July Euro area balance of payments \par 0830 GMT UK:          2Q Bank of England on U.K. banks external claims \par 0900 GMT EU:          July construction output \par 1230 GMT US:          August consumer price index \par 1355 GMT US:          September Thomson Reuters/University of Michigan \par                       survey of consumers - preliminary \par  \par  \par TOP HEADLINES - Dow Jones/WSJ \par BOJ EXPECTS CURRENT ACCOUNT BALANCE AT Y17.10 TLN FRI VS Y15.09 TLN THU \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan's latest forecast showed it expects its current account balance to increase by Y2 trillion Friday, indicating that it doesn't plan, at least for now, to soak up the yen that the government sold Wednesday in its massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 2317 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ SKIPS 0030 GMT MARKET OP; SUGGESTS LEAVES SOME \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FUNDS IN MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  skipped its Friday morning money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , refraining--as expected--from draining any funds from the market. (published 0034 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NODA: WILL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET IF NEEDED \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Friday the government will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to tame the yen's strength if necessary, emphasizing his resolve to prevent any unduly sharp rises in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0116 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN PM TAPS BANRI KAIEDA AS ECON MINISTER - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan is considering choosing Committee on Financial Affairs Chairman Banri Kaieda to serve as economy minister in revamped Cabinet, the Asahi Shimbun reported Friday. (published 0152 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IMF: BANK INDONESIA'S MONETARY POLICY STANCE APPROPRIATE FOR NOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia's current monetary policy stance is appropriate given that inflation is within the target range and the risk that hiking rates now could attract more volatile portfolio capital, the International Monetary Fund said Friday. (published 0200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO LAUNCH \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MEASURES BY END-SEPT - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to introduce measures by the end of this month to prevent excessive strength in the baht, Thai-language daily Post Today reported Friday, citing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board member Satit Rungkasiri. (published 0137 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =4TH UPDATE: ORACLE 1Q PROFIT UP 20% ON HIGHER REVENUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oracle Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s fiscal first-quarter profit grew 20% as the business-software giant benefited from new revenue from its \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sun Microsystems\f28 \uc2 \f2  acquisition, as well as strong demand for software licenses. (published 0038 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LG GROUP\f28 \uc2 \f2 : \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG ELECTRONICS\f28 \uc2 \f2  CHIEF EXECUTIVE NAM YONG TO RESIGN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chief executive of \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG Electronics\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the world's third-largest cellphone maker by shipments, has offered to resign, taking responsibility for the company's recent weak performance, \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0125 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ACS TAKEOVER OF LEIGHTON UNLIKELY; STRATEGY MAY CHANGE -ANALYSTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A proposed takeover of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Leighton Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s German parent \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hochtief AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  by Spain's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Actividades de Construccion y Servicios S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 . isn't likely to trigger a full takeover of the Australian construction company but could mean a change of strategy, analysts said Friday. (published 2334 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW: SUNVIC CHEMICAL EYES RECORD ANNUAL PROFIT AS SALES PRICES GROW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 09-16-10 2308ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SunVic Chemical Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is on track for a record profit in 2010 on the back of higher selling prices, and earnings growth is set to remain robust in coming years helped by cost savings. (published 0117 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TOP HEADLINES - Indian Media \par India Plan Panel Official: Inflation To Slow On Foodgrain Output, Not Rates - PTI \par India Minister Rules Out Change In Realty Foreign Direct Investment Lock-in - The Hindu \par Airtel In Talks With Rivals For Partnership To Offer 3G Services - Business Line \par  \f28 \par \par \