\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Govt Mulls Boosting Funds For  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  - Kyodo\b0\par\par\uc2 372 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 13:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 The Japanese government is considering increasing funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in anticipation of a prolonged \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the yen for dollars, Kyodo News reported Thursday, citing sources familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The increase is expected to demonstrate the government's determination to prevent the yen from rising further, after the government Wednesday conducted its first yen-selling, dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in six and a half years, they said.\par \par \uc2 After Wednesday's Y2 trillion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's biggest daily yen-selling, dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the government appeared poised to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market further.\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Naoto Kan reiterated Thursday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to sell the yen when necessary, saying it will take "decisive steps" to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surge, which threatens the nation's export-oriented economy.\par \par \uc2 The government usually issues \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund bills to raise funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Under the fiscal 2010 budget that caps outstanding \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund bills at Y145 trillion, the government may be able to issue up to Y35 trillion more in such bills in addition to about Y110 trillion outstanding at the end of June for refinancing.\par \par \uc2 The sum for fiscal 2010 ending next March indicates the government will be able to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  close to an annual record of Y32.9 trillion reached in fiscal 2003.\par \par \uc2 If the daily pace of Y2 trillion as seen Wednesday continues for some time, however, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds may be depleted.\par \par \uc2 The government is considering raising the cap on outstanding \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund bills under an extra budget for fiscal 2010 or a principal budget for fiscal 2011.\par \par \uc2 In another way to raise funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the government could effectively borrow funds from the Bank of Japan through sales of U.S. Treasury securities holdings to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  under repurchase agreements.\par \par \uc2 The government adopted the measure to secure \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds before an extra budget was approved to raise the cap on outstanding \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund bills in 2004.\par \par \uc2 -Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2900\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 16, 2010 07:55 ET (11:55 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100916e69g002i8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
