\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Facing Pressure To Do More After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Megumi Fujikawa  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 835 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 17:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday gave a boost to the Japanese government's move into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to curb the yen's rise, but now it is facing pressure to do even more to prop up the economy.\par \par \uc2 The notoriously conservative \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took the unusual step of allowing the estimated $21 billion generated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain in the banking system. Normally when there is such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the cash is taken out by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  through daily money-market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . By allowing the funds to remain in the system, the BOJ has effectively offered the economy another boost.\par \par \uc2 Pressure on the bank that was previously seen on the fringes of the political agenda is now moving front and center. Ironically, a man now in the political wilderness may be the one to give the issue new urgency.\par \par \uc2 Democratic Party power broker Ichiro Ozawa, who lost to Prime Minister Naoto Kan in a party-leadership vote Tuesday, for the first time has suggested the landmark 1997 Bank of Japan law should be reviewed. The legislation gave the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  independence from the powerful \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and critics see any changes to the law as undermining the bank's authority.\par \par \uc2 Adding to this, a group of Democratic Party lawmakers met Thursday to urge the BOJ to take additional steps to complement the potential "kick-start" from the lower yen. "It is important that the BOJ implement monetary easing on a major scale to sustain the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the group said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The calls echo remarks from private-sector economists who blame the BOJ directly for Japan's continued economic problems. The bank has been accused of dragging its feet on taking the bold steps needed to get Japan out of its deflationary period that has lasted more than 10 years.\par \par \uc2 Richard Jerram, chief economist at Macquarie Capital Securities Japan, said recently that, while independence is normally very important for a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the BOJ has done too little to tackle Japan's problems. "You can argue that BOJ independence hasn't served Japan well over the past 12 to 15 years," he said.\par \par \uc2 BOJ Governor Masaaki Shirakawa has strongly defended the bank's policies, which he said already have gone well beyond the usual tools of monetary policy--including a zero-interest-rate policy, purchase of government bonds and targeting prices to end deflation.\par \par \uc2 In a speech Thursday to a BOJ-sponsored institute, he said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had "invented various unconventional policy measures out of necessity," and that such measures had been highly effective in combating the effects of the recent financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 He and other officials have argued that the bank alone can't solve the structural problems caused by a shrinking work force and by government policies that have created huge budget deficits yet failed to stimulate growth.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the government of Kan surprised the markets by launching a massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stop the steady rise in the yen that threatened Japan's export-driven economy.\par \par \uc2 Kan had just survived an attempted ouster by a political rival the day before and was thought to be immersed in a cabinet reshuffle. Vice Finance Minister Motohisa Ikeda said he was satisfied with the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 's outcome, which pushed the yen down some 3.5%.\par \par \uc2 Ikeda told reporters that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't run out of money to continue the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign, suggesting authorities were prepared for a long showdown against speculators in the world's largest financial market, where $4 trillion changes hands daily.\par \par \uc2 He added that he expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help out.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , already under pressure from the government and markets, held a special session on Aug. 30 to expand a special lending program to banks to make available up to 30 trillion yen--10 trillion yen in six-month loans and 20 trillion yen in three-month funds--at a rock-bottom rate of 0.1%. But critics said the move would do little since banks already had plenty of money and needed borrowers instead.\par \par \uc2 RuiXue Xu, rates strategist at RBS Securities Japan, said it was now likely that "the government will put more pressure on the BOJ to take more easing steps" at the next policy meeting scheduled for Oct. 4 and 5.\par \par \uc2 One question is what exactly the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can--and should--do with short-term rates locked at near-zero and with a large surplus of funding already in the banking system.\par \par \uc2 Bank Governor Shirakawa said Thursday that it is one thing to act when an economy is suffering "acute pain" and another when it is in "chronic illness."\par \par \uc2 -By Megumi Fujikawa, Dow Jones Newswires; megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Hiroshi Miwa contributed to this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 16, 2010 11:06 ET (15:06 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100916e69g003mc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
