\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Summary Of US Stocks\b0\par\par\uc2 1,370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2010\par 00:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 2228 GMT [Dow Jones] WALL STREET: Technology companies boosted stocks as confidence mounted economy would avoid double-dip recession; \uc2 Hewlett-Packard\uc2  rose 1.8%, Cisco Systems gained 1.6%, Intel +1.3%; "It seems like we priced in too much of a double dip, and it's not coming to pass as bad as people anticipated," says Patrick Becker Jr., principal at Becker Capital Management. Industrials weakened, weighed by 3.8% drop in \uc2 FedEx\uc2  after 1Q profit more than doubled on rise in revenue, but company forecast 2Q earnings below analysts' average estimate. Company also said will combine FedEx Freight, \uc2 FedEx National LTL\b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  at end of January, as it cuts 1,700 full-time employees, closes 100 facilities. Shipping peer \uc2 United Parcel Service\uc2  also fell 1.4%. \uc2 Ford Motor\uc2  added 4.8% after car maker upgraded to "overweight" from "equal weight" by \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 , which said North American market will sustain strong margins. Dow +0.2%, Nasdaq up 0.1%, Philly semicons +0.8%. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2225 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Westpac\uc2  says it's time to buy USD/JPY, EUR/JPY on Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "While we await balance sheet data from the (Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to confirm the size of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that it has not been sterilized, we take the move at face value and shift our bias to buy in both." USD/JPY last 85.815, EUR/JPY last 112.215. (enda.curran@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2225 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Westpac\uc2  says it's time to buy USD/JPY, EUR/JPY on Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "While we await balance sheet data from the (Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to confirm the size of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that it has not been sterilized, we take the move at face value and shift our bias to buy in both." USD/JPY last 85.815, EUR/JPY last 112.215. (enda.curran@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2217 GMT [Dow Jones] AUD/USD may come under pressure in Asia with profit-taking likely in a slightly over extended market, says Jonathan Cavenagh, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Westpac\uc2 . Says focus has switched to next week's FOMC meeting against a somewhat improved picture for the U.S. economy. Says equity markets seem to be treading water until then, so leads for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like AUD will be limited. Says heightened speculation surrounding a rate hike in October is overdone, and some support will be withdrawn from AUD/USD as markets realise the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has more time on its hands. Expects solid support on dips down to 0.9300. Now 0.9360. (james.glynn@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2213 GMT [Dow Jones] NZD/AUD could tumble in coming sessions on back of RBNZ's bearish outlook, fair value in 0.7500-0.7700 range, support around 0.7155, says Bank of New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategist Mike Jones. Pair last 0.7736. "We wouldn't be surprised to see NZD/AUD continue to slide in coming sessions." (enda.curran@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2209 GMT [Dow Jones] U.S. SUMMARY: USD held sharp gains against JPY after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strangle recent strength in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's estimated Y2 trillion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  left \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors cautious, with Japanese officials saying more action could be on table to stem JPY's strength, a stance that might have also given a boost to EUR, says Steven Englander, head of G10 strategy at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  in New York; "If the market becomes convinced that [Japan] will be resisting U.S. dollar weakness against the yen, other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will become more attractive as U.S. dollar alternatives," he said. EUR/USD at 1.3085 late Thursday vs 1.3012 late Wednesday, USD/JPY at 85.81 vs 85.63, EUR/JPY at 112.29 vs 111.36, GBP/USD at 1.5635 vs 1.5623, USD/CHF at 1.0146 vs 1.0035, USD Index at 81.224 vs 81.453. Treasurys maturing in five or more years fell, hurt by selling related to new corporate and government agency debt supply; 2-year yields flat at 0.480%, 10-year yields +4.3 bps at 2.766%. Tech concerns boosted stocks as confidence mounted economy would avoid double-dip recession; \uc2 Hewlett-Packard\uc2  rose 1.8%, while Cisco Systems gained 1.6%, Intel added 1.3%; Dow +0.2%, Nasdaq up 0.1%, Philly semicons +0.8%. Gold futures posted new record settlement, as USD weakened, investors wanted more of precious metal as haven; December Comex gold rose $5.10 to $1,273.80/oz. Crude oil futures prices dropped as scheduled restart of a major pipeline rekindled oversupply concerns in world's biggest oil consumer; October Nymex crude settled down $1.45, at $74.57/bbl. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2155 GMT [Dow Jones] NZX-50 likely touch higher on U.S. lead, weaker NZD, says \uc2 Craigs Investment Partners\uc2  broker James Porteous; "The New Zealand dollar is a little bit weaker, which bodes well for exporters." NZD/USD may support Fisher & Paykel Healthcare (FPH.NZ), Rakon (RAK.NZ). Says dearth of local news means market lacking cues. Comments reported by Fairfax owned Stuff website from \uc2 Air NZ\uc2  (AIR.NZ) chief executive \uc2 Rob Fyfe\uc2  saying needs alliance with Virgin Blue to continue to be competitive on Tasman route may weigh on stock. NZX-50 closed flat yesterday at 3195.63. (lucy.craymer@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2136 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD likely to be well supported in Asian session as fears of European debt crisis fading further into background. But \uc2 HSBC\uc2  NZ Chief Manager Daniel Brdanovic notes market will have one eye on USD/JPY to see if anything happens there after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; "the market is a little bit wary." EUR/USD last 1.3077 vs 1.3085 late NY, tips support at 1.3035-1.3050, resistance at 1.3150; "Asia will treat it as a buy the dips, so there is still some upside pressure." (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2115 GMT [Dow Jones] NZ government bonds, IRS unchanged early as market waits for large government bond tender later in day, says local bond trader. Debt Management Office to offer NZ$200 million April 2015s, NZ$75 million December 2017s, NZ$150 million May 2021s. Trader says bonds well bid in recent days, expects tender to go off well. Adds swaps rallied harder than bonds yields yesterday as market waiting for tender; 2-year swap rates unchanged at 3.75%, 10-year swaps unchanged at 4.96%, Nov 2011s yields unchanged at 3.61%. (lucy.craymer@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2029 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  retains year-end target of 0.6800 on NZD/USD, last 0.7244. Says local issues such as recent finance company collapse, rebuilding after Christchurch earthquake should weigh on NZD; "RBNZ is on hold for the near-term, the data flow out of Australia has been superior, and local events such as the collapse of SCF and the earthquake are on balance NZD negative." Tips further NZD under-performance next year as RBA forges away with tightening cycle. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2013 GMT [Dow Jones] Simon Lewis, previously official spokesman for former U.K. Prime Minister Gordon Brown, taking over as chief executive for the Association for Financial Markets in Europe, a lobbying group for the financial services industry. Lewis, who also worked in public relations for \uc2 Vodafone\uc2  and Buckingham Palace, takes over CEO role from Mark Austen, AFME's head of markets policy who will become chief operating officer. Lewis takes the job Oct. 1. (jacob.bunge@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2010 GMT [Dow Jones] The New York Fed's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap program remains lightly utilized. The ECB rolled over the $60 million it drew a week ago, and the Bank of Japan saw $3 million of the $4 million it borrowed maturing, leaving total outstanding at $61 million. Demand for dollar liquidity among the world's major \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be without problems, hence the minimal activity. (michael.derby@dowjones.com) [ 09-16-10 1828ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100916e69g000en\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
